S T R I N G F U N C T I O N
getBytes() and toCharArray() b[]
DEFINITION
getBytes() converts a String into a byte array using the 
default ASCII/8-bit character-to-byte encoding. 
toCharArray() converts every character of a String into a char 
array.
SYNTAX
byte[] getBytes()
char[] toCharArray()
CODE SNIPPET
String str = "abcdef";
byte b[] = str.getBytes();
for (byte bt : b) 
 System.out.print(bt + " ");
char c[] = str.toCharArray();
for (char cr : c) 
 System.out.print(cr);
OUTPUT
97 98 99 100 101 102
abcdef

S T R I N G C O M P A R I S O N
== vs equals() cmp
DEFINITION
equals() compares character content; 
== compares object references — whether two variables point to 
the exact same object in memory.
SYNTAX
str1 == str2
equals(): compares characters ==: compares references
CODE SNIPPET
String s1 = new String("Hello");
String s2 = s1;
String s3 = new String(s1);
System.out.println(s1.equals(s2));
System.out.println(s1 == s2);
System.out.println(s1.equals(s3));
System.out.println(s1 == s3);
OUTPUT
true
true
true
false

