Searching Strings — indexOf() & lastIndexOf() find
DEFINITION
indexOf() finds the first occurrence of a character or substring; 
lastIndexOf() finds the last occurrence. If nothing matches, both 
return −1.
SYNTAX
int indexOf(char ch)
int lastIndexOf(char ch)
int indexOf(String str)
int lastIndexOf(String str)
CODE SNIPPET
String str = "abcabdef";
System.out.println(str.indexOf('a'));
System.out.println(str.lastIndexOf('a'));
String str2 = "abcabdefabcswabd";
System.out.println(str2.indexOf("abd"));
String str3 = "abcabdefabcswd";
System.out.println(str3.lastIndexOf("abc"));
OUTPUT
0 3 3 8
